  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.uiowa.edu/faculty/view/75237": {
      "title": "ACADEMIC OBGYN LABORIST",
      "description": "ACADEMIC OBGYN LABORIST Requisition # 75237 Position Basics Type of Position CLINICAL-TRACK Advertising Ends on: Extended Until Position is Filled Advertising Started on: Friday, May 24th, 2024 College: Carver College of Medicine Department: Obstetrics & Gynecology Salary Salary: Commensurate Position Details Full/Part Time Status: Negotiable Position Description: The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Iowa is seeking a physician for an Academic OBGYN Laborist position in the Division of General Obstetrics and Gynecology. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate to qualifications and experience. Responsibilities will include instruction and supervision of resident physicians and medical students. During shifts on Labor and Delivery, this physician will lead a team that provides safe, high-quality, cost-effective obstetrical care using evidence-based medicine and best practices. The multi-disciplinary obstetric team includes OB/GYN generalists, Maternal Fetal Medicine specialists, Certified Nurse Midwives, Nurse Practitioners, Family Medicine obstetric providers, Residents and Fellows. This role will be based at the Medical Center on the University Campus managing the obstetric unit, staffing triage, labor management, and deliveries including operative deliveries. The position includes rounding on antepartum and postpartum patients, providing obstetric and gynecologic consultations to the inpatient and emergency departments, consulting for family practice obstetric providers and advanced practice providers. There are opportunities to be involved in obstetric quality and safety initiatives and committees. A 1.0 cFTE position would require 12 shifts monthly (12 hours each) with opportunities to pick up additional shifts for additional compensation. Successful candidates will be required to self-disclose any misconduct history or pending research misconduct investigation including but not limited to sexual misconduct in prior employment and provide a related release and will be subject to a criminal background and credential check. Education Requirement: Successful candidates must possess a medical degree (MD) or equivalent. This position requires completion of an ACGME-accredited residency in obstetrics and gynecology. Required Qualifications: Required qualifications include excellent clinical and surgical skills, excellent skills in patient management, strong oral and written communication skills, demonstrated teaching skills, and commitment to team culture. The applicant will be required to have licensure eligibility by the Iowa Board of Medicine and will be required to be licensed by the Iowa Board of Medicine before commencement of employment. Certifications: Certifications include American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology active candidate/board certification in Obstetrics and Gynecology. Desirable Qualifications: Experience in teaching and practicing in a busy obstetric practice. Online Application Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Name and Contact Information of References Letter of Interest Number of References: 3 To start the Online Application process for this position, click the \"Apply for This Position\" button located below the Contact Information. Contact Information Contact: Miriam E Murray - miriam-murray@uiowa.edu Cmed-Obstetrics/Gynecology Pomerantz Family Pavilion 720 Melrose Avenue 51210 PFP Iowa City, IA 52242 Phone: 319-356-7072 The University of Iowa is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment free from discrimination on the basis of race, creed, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, pregnancy (including childbirth and related conditions), disability, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, service in the U.S. military, sexual orientation, or associational preferences. Persons with disabilities may contact University Human Resources/Faculty and Staff Disability Services, (319) 335-2660 or fsds@uiowa.edu , to inquire or discuss accommodation needs. Prospective employees may review the University Campus Security Policy and the latest annual crime statistics by contacting the Department of Public Safety at 319/335-5022. The University of Iowa University of Iowa Jobs @ UIowa Iowa City, Iowa 52242 319-335-3500 Footer primary Human Resources Working at a Public University Federal EEO Rights Campus Safety & Security Contact Us © 2026 The University of Iowa Privacy Notice UI Nondiscrimination Statement Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.uiowa.edu/faculty/view/75763": {
      "title": "ACADEMIC SURGICAL PATHOLOGIST",
      "description": "ACADEMIC SURGICAL PATHOLOGIST Requisition # 75763 Position Basics Type of Position TENURE-TRACK/CLINICAL Advertising Ends on: Extended Until Position is Filled Advertising Started on: Monday, October 6th, 2025 College: Carver College of Medicine Department: Pathology Salary Salary: Commensurate Position Details Full/Part Time Status: Full Time Position Description: The University of Iowa Department of Pathology seeks surgical pathologists with subspecialty expertise to join a collegial group of academic pathologists. We are an active surgical pathology division that is sub-specialty focused and covers a growing network of hospitals and clinics in eastern Iowa, with >60,000 cases annually. Candidates will be considered on either the non-tenure clinical track or tenure track at assistant, associate, or professor level. Sub-specialty training and/or experience in breast pathology, genitourinary pathology, gastrointestinal pathology, or thoracic pathology is desired; cytopathology training/experience would be an added benefit but not necessary. In our model, faculty would cover one or more surgical pathology subspecialties. Faculty will participate in training of pathology residents, fellows, and medical students and will have abundant opportunities to pursue clinical/translational research. Successful candidates will be required to self-disclose any misconduct history or pending research misconduct investigation including but not limited to sexual misconduct in prior employment and provide a related release and will be subject to a criminal background and credential check. Education Requirement: MD or equivalent Graduation from an accredited Anatomic Pathology or Anatomic Pathology/ Clinical Pathology residency program Fellowship training or equivalent experience/expertise in general or sub-specialty surgical pathology Certifications: Board certification in Anatomic Pathology or Anatomic Pathology/Clinical Pathology with credentials required to obtain a medical license in the State of Iowa Desirable Qualifications: Experience, fellowship training, or demonstrated interest in breast pathology, genitourinary pathology, gastrointestinal pathology, or thoracic pathology Excellent skills in practical surgical pathology >2 years of academic experience Demonstrated ability to excel at scholarship and teaching Evidence of leadership potential Online Application Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Name and Contact Information of References Letter of Interest Supporting Attachments Number of References: 3 To start the Online Application process for this position, click the \"Apply for This Position\" button located below the Contact Information. Contact Information Contact: Jessica R Schnoebelen Cmed-Pathology General Hospital 220 Hawkins Drive C660 GH Iowa City, IA 52242 Phone: 319-384-9609 The University of Iowa is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment free from discrimination on the basis of race, creed, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, pregnancy (including childbirth and related conditions), disability, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, service in the U.S. military, sexual orientation, or associational preferences. Persons with disabilities may contact University Human Resources/Faculty and Staff Disability Services, (319) 335-2660 or fsds@uiowa.edu , to inquire or discuss accommodation needs. Prospective employees may review the University Campus Security Policy and the latest annual crime statistics by contacting the Department of Public Safety at 319/335-5022. The University of Iowa University of Iowa Jobs @ UIowa Iowa City, Iowa 52242 319-335-3500 Footer primary Human Resources Working at a Public University Federal EEO Rights Campus Safety & Security Contact Us © 2026 The University of Iowa Privacy Notice UI Nondiscrimination Statement Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.uiowa.edu/faculty/view/75187": {
      "title": "ADOLESCENT MEDICINE PHYSICIAN",
      "description": "ADOLESCENT MEDICINE PHYSICIAN Requisition # 75187 Position Basics Type of Position OTHER Advertising Ends on: Extended Until Position is Filled Advertising Started on: Thursday, March 28th, 2024 College: Carver College of Medicine Department: Pediatrics Salary Salary: Commensurate Position Details Full/Part Time Status: Negotiable Position Description: University of Iowa Stead Family Department of Pediatrics seeks an Adolescent Medicine Physician. Appointment rank is open and may be to either the tenure track or clinical (non-tenure) track consistent with clinical experience and research interest. Appointment rank to Instructor of Pediatrics (non-tenure or clinical track) may also be considered. The individual selected will join the Division of General Pediatrics and Adolescent Medicine to provide patient care, teaching, and consultative services as a pediatrician specializing in Adolescent Medicine. The University of Iowa Roy J. and Lucille A. Carver College of Medicine is one of the nation’s top medical schools. It is ranked No. 44 in research in the 2024 U.S. News & World Report listing of “Best Graduate Schools,” and it is ranked No. 23 in National Institutes of Health funding among public institutions by the Blue Ridge Institute for Medical Research. The UI Stead Family Department of Pediatrics is currently ranked No. 25 in NIH funding among all public pediatric departments nationwide. The UI Stead Family Department of Pediatrics comprises the medical staff of UI Stead Family Children’s Hospital, Iowa’s only nationally ranked children’s hospital and home to the state’s only accredited Level 1 Regional Resource Pediatric Trauma Center. The ACGME-accredited pediatric residency program at UI Stead Family Children’s Hospital trains 50 pediatric resident physicians. For its 2023-24 edition of “Best Children’s Hospitals,” U.S. News & World Report ranked UI Stead Family Children's Hospital in six pediatric specialties: neonatology, diabetes and endocrinology, nephrology, neurology and neurosurgery, orthopedics, and urology. For more information contact: Rami Boutros, MD, MBA Clinical Professor of Pediatrics Division Director, General Pediatrics and Adolescent Medicine Executive Medical Director, Off-site Ambulatory Programs rami-boutros@uiowa.edu Visit us on the web at: www.uichildrens.org Successful candidates will be required to self-disclose any misconduct history or pending research misconduct investigation including but not limited to sexual misconduct in prior employment and provide a related release and will be subject to a criminal background and credential check. This applies to clinical, tenure and research positions. Education Requirement: Must hold an MD/DO degree, or equivalent Required Qualifications: Board certified or eligible in adolescent medicine, or equivalent License or eligible for licensure in the State of Iowa Tenure track candidates must demonstrate evidence of scholarly investigation Desirable Qualifications: Interest and/or expertise in eating disorder Clinical experience in the care of adolescents in an academic setting Experience in patient-oriented research Teaching competence in pediatrics for medical students and residents Evidence of scholarly activity Strong oral and written communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrated experience working effectively in a welcoming and respectful workplace environment Online Application Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Interest To start the Online Application process for this position, click the \"Apply for This Position\" button located below the Contact Information. Contact Information Contact: Jeanie Cromer - jeanie-cromer@uiowa.edu Cmed-Pediatrics General Hospital 220 Hawkins Drive GH Iowa City, IA 52242 The University of Iowa is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment free from discrimination on the basis of race, creed, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, pregnancy (including childbirth and related conditions), disability, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, service in the U.S. military, sexual orientation, or associational preferences. Persons with disabilities may contact University Human Resources/Faculty and Staff Disability Services, (319) 335-2660 or fsds@uiowa.edu , to inquire or discuss accommodation needs. Prospective employees may review the University Campus Security Policy and the latest annual crime statistics by contacting the Department of Public Safety at 319/335-5022. The University of Iowa University of Iowa Jobs @ UIowa Iowa City, Iowa 52242 319-335-3500 Footer primary Human Resources Working at a Public University Federal EEO Rights Campus Safety & Security Contact Us © 2026 The University of Iowa Privacy Notice UI Nondiscrimination Statement Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.uiowa.edu/faculty/view/76052": {
      "title": "ADULT - GERO PRIMARY CARE NURSE PRACTITIONER",
      "description": "ADULT - GERO PRIMARY CARE NURSE PRACTITIONER Requisition # 76052 Position Basics Type of Position OTHER Advertising Ends on: Extended Until Position is Filled Advertising Started on: Friday, October 9th, 2026 College: College of Nursing Department: Nursing Salary Salary: Commensurate Position Details Full/Part Time Status: Negotiable Position Description: Position Type: Negotiable, Other Salary: Commensurate with experience and qualifications. Percent of Effort: 50-100% Rank and responsibilities: will be aligned with each candidate’s educational background and clinical expertise. Location: Position required to be performed in-person at the College of Nursing on the University of Iowa Campus The University of Iowa College of Nursing seeks applications for a faculty position (open rank and track) with expertise in adult–gerontology primary care advanced practice nursing. This is an academic-year (9-month) appointment, with effort and rank commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications and experience. Opportunities for clinical practice engagement may be available and supported as part of the appointment. Position Overview Faculty in this role will contribute to the College’s teaching, clinical practice, service, and professional productivity missions. The successful candidate will participate in a collaborative, interdisciplinary academic environment, preparing undergraduate and graduate students for leadership in complex healthcare systems and advancing innovations in patient care and education. Teaching Responsibilities Teach primarily in the Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) program through classroom, clinical, simulation, and/or laboratory instruction. Teaching responsibilities may also include MSN and BSN nursing students based on departmental needs and faculty expertise. Integrate active learning strategies and evidence-based teaching approaches Promote development of critical thinking, clinical judgment, decision-making, and professional values Supervise and mentor students in clinical and academic settings Contribute to curriculum development and program evaluation Practice & Clinical Engagement Maintain current clinical practice expertise aligned with adult–gerontology primary care Support integration of clinical expertise into teaching and curriculum Contribute to strengthening academic–practice partnerships and community engagement initiatives Service & Professional Contributions Participate in college, university, and professional service activities Contribute to programmatic initiatives and interdisciplinary collaboration Engage in professional productivity (e.g., scholarship, presentations, policy contributions), consistent with rank and track Successful candidates will be required to self-disclose any misconduct history or pending research misconduct investigation, including but not limited to sexual misconduct in prior employment, and provide a related release. Final candidates will be subject to criminal background and credential checks. If your H-1B petition is subject to the September 19, 2025, Presidential Proclamation, please note that the department will not cover the $100,000 payment associated with H-1B sponsorship, either at the time of hire or for international travel purposes. We encourage impacted individuals to explore alternative pathways for work authorization. The Immigration Services office is available to help identify options that may be suitable for your situation. About the College The University of Iowa College of Nursing is a nationally recognized leader in nursing education, research, and practice innovation. Faculty collaborate closely with University of Iowa Health Care and benefit from access to state-of-the-art clinical simulation environments and strong academic–practice partnerships. Application Information Applicants should submit: A letter of interest describing teaching, clinical, and scholarly experience Curriculum vitae Contact information for three professional references Successful candidates will be required to complete a background check and disclose any prior misconduct history, consistent with University policy. Education Requirement: Earned doctorate in nursing or related field (or terminal degree appropriate to track); Candidates with a terminal degree in another discipline may be considered if they also hold an MSN with an Adult-Gerontology Primary Care Nurse Practitioner focus and meet all other position requirements. Required Qualifications: Eligibility for or current advanced practice board certification in adult or adult–gerontology primary care Demonstrated experience or strong potential in teaching graduate students Clinical expertise in adult–gerontology or primary care nursing Strong written and verbal communication skills, and interpersonal skills; demonstrated by the ability to effectively transmit, receive, and accurately interpret ideas, information and needs through appropriate communication methods and behaviors to provide excellent customer service and maintain working relationships. Eligibility and ability to obtain and maintain licensure as a Registered Nurse and Advanced Registered Nurse Practitioner in the State of Iowa. Selected candidate must complete the State of Iowa Registered Nurse licensure process upon appointment. Desirable Qualifications: Experience in curriculum design, simulation, or clinical education Evidence of scholarship or professional productivity consistent with rank Previous experience in lab or simulation Active clinical practice role aligned with adult–gerontology primary care advanced practice nursing. Online Application Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Name and Contact Information of References Letter of Interest Number of References: 3 To start the Online Application process for this position, click the \"Apply for This Position\" button located below the Contact Information. Contact Information Contact: Daniel J Crawford - daniel-j-crawford@uiowa.edu Cnur-Nursing College of Nursing Building 50 Newton Road 237 CNB Iowa City, IA 52242-1121 Department URL: https://nursing.uiowa.edu/ The University of Iowa is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment free from discrimination on the basis of race, creed, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, pregnancy (including childbirth and related conditions), disability, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, service in the U.S. military, sexual orientation, or associational preferences. Persons with disabilities may contact University Human Resources/Faculty and Staff Disability Services, (319) 335-2660 or fsds@uiowa.edu , to inquire or discuss accommodation needs. Prospective employees may review the University Campus Security Policy and the latest annual crime statistics by contacting the Department of Public Safety at 319/335-5022. The University of Iowa University of Iowa Jobs @ UIowa Iowa City, Iowa 52242 319-335-3500 Footer primary Human Resources Working at a Public University Federal EEO Rights Campus Safety & Security Contact Us © 2026 The University of Iowa Privacy Notice UI Nondiscrimination Statement Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.uiowa.edu/faculty/view/75915": {
      "title": "ADULT HOSPITALIST - MEDICAL DIRECTOR MCD",
      "description": "ADULT HOSPITALIST - MEDICAL DIRECTOR MCD Requisition # 75915 Position Basics Type of Position CLINICAL-TRACK Advertising Ends on: Extended Until Position is Filled Advertising Started on: Friday, May 8th, 2026 College: Carver College of Medicine Department: Internal Medicine Salary Salary: Commensurate Position Details Full/Part Time Status: Full Time Position Description: The University of Iowa Department of Internal Medicine is seeking faculty for a leadership position in The Division of Hospital Medicine, Adult Hospitalist Program as the Medical Site Director for UI Medical Center Downtown campus. This role will be a 1.0 position, with 25% administrative time to lead the UI Health Care Medical Center Downtown Campus Hospitalist team. This leadership role offers a unique opportunity to serve in a community hospital affiliated with largest academic institution and quaternary referral center of the State of Iowa. This campus is a 120-bed hospital located in the heart of downtown Iowa City and the University Iowa, and just one mile away from the main campus. This is an exciting opportunity to lead and grow a group of outstanding and committed clinicians that provided an invaluable service to the community. Leadership responsibilities will include supporting physicians and Advance Practice Providers in delivering 24-hour inpatient care at the Medical Center Downtown, serve as primary Hospital Medicine representative in hospital committees, collaborating with Hospital Medicine Division leadership on supporting faculty recruitment and development initiatives, as well as fostering opportunities for scholarship, research, and education in the downtown campus. Appointment rank will be at the Clinical Assistant, Clinical Associate or Clinical Professor (non-tenure track) level commensurate with the candidate’s former rank and or experience. Our campus is also part of a leading academic system committed to changing medicine and healthcare. WHO WE ARE The hospital medicine team at the Medical Center Downtown campus is a growing physician group that has been operating since 2006 composed of both Internal Medicine and Family Medicine-trained physicians. We practice within a hospital located in downtown Iowa City that has provided care for the community for 150 years and act as a referral center for critical access and other local Hospitals. We pride ourselves on high quality, evidence-based care, working within a strong and experienced healthcare team, with excellent subspecialist and administrative support. Our team includes physicians, advanced practice providers, nurses, clinical pharmacists, and administrative staff to support our clinical operations. We provide opportunities for mentorship and career development as part of the Division of Hospital Medicine within the Department of Internal Medicine at the University of Iowa. BENEFITS Competitive salary with exceptional benefits including excellent retirement plan with 2:1 employer match (up to 10%), health, dental, life and disability insurance. Up to 10% bonus potential based on quality and productivity measures Relocation and/or transitional bonus payments Access to a thriving, innovative academic environment with multiple lectures, CME opportunities, grand rounds, among others. Opportunities for career advancement and leadership development including: Participating in the UIHC Executive Leadership Academy Opportunities for pursuing advanced degrees (MBA, MPH, or similar) Malpractice Insurance The University of Iowa is located in Iowa City, a vibrant community located in the rolling hills of southeastern Iowa. One of four UNESCO Cities of Literature, the Iowa City community offers outstanding schools, quality entertainment, literary, musical and cultural opportunities, outdoor recreation and Big Ten sporting events. Learn more about Iowa City and the Department of Internal Medicine by watching the video: https://medicine.uiowa.edu/internalmedicine/about-us/why-iowa Successful candidates will be required to self-disclose any misconduct history or pending research misconduct investigation including but not limited to sexual misconduct in prior employment and provide a related releasee and will be subject to a criminal background and credential check. Education Requirement: Candidates must have an M.D. degree or equivalent Completion of an ACGME-accredited Residency Program Required Qualifications: Excellent Communication Skills Three or more years of Hospital Medicine experience Professional experience working effectively with individuals from a variety of backgrounds and perspectives Certifications: Board certified or eligible in Internal Medicine or Family Practice Desirable Qualifications: Experience in a formal physician leadership role Online Application Required Documents Curriculum Vitae To start the Online Application process for this position, click the \"Apply for This Position\" button located below the Contact Information. Contact Information Contact: Alyssa N Conrad - alyssa-n-conrad@uiowa.edu Cmed-Internal Medicine General Hospital 220 Hawkins Drive SE 636-1 GH Iowa City, IA 52242 The University of Iowa is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment free from discrimination on the basis of race, creed, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, pregnancy (including childbirth and related conditions), disability, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, service in the U.S. military, sexual orientation, or associational preferences. Persons with disabilities may contact University Human Resources/Faculty and Staff Disability Services, (319) 335-2660 or fsds@uiowa.edu , to inquire or discuss accommodation needs. Prospective employees may review the University Campus Security Policy and the latest annual crime statistics by contacting the Department of Public Safety at 319/335-5022. The University of Iowa University of Iowa Jobs @ UIowa Iowa City, Iowa 52242 319-335-3500 Footer primary Human Resources Working at a Public University Federal EEO Rights Campus Safety & Security Contact Us © 2026 The University of Iowa Privacy Notice UI Nondiscrimination Statement Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.uiowa.edu/faculty/view/75501": {
      "title": "ADULT HOSPITALIST, DOWNTOWN CAMPUS",
      "description": "ADULT HOSPITALIST, DOWNTOWN CAMPUS Requisition # 75501 Position Basics Type of Position OTHER Advertising Ends on: Extended Until Position is Filled Advertising Started on: Friday, December 27th, 2024 College: Carver College of Medicine Department: Internal Medicine Salary Salary: Commensurate Position Details Full/Part Time Status: Negotiable Position Description: The University of Iowa Department of Internal Medicine is seeking faculty for a position(s) in The Division of General Internal Medicine, Adult Hospitalist Program. Appointment rank will be at the Instructor (non-track) level. The Hospitalist Program offers extensive opportunities for clinicians to practice in a community hospital setting located in the heart of downtown Iowa City. Our campus is also part of a leading academic system committed to changing medicine and healthcare. Education Requirement: Candidates must have an M.D. degree or equivalent. Completion of an ACGME-accredited Residency Program Required Qualifications: Board certified or eligible in Internal Medicine or Family Practice Excellent communication skills Ability to work collaboratively within a healthcare team Certifications: Board certified or eligible in Internal Medicine or Family Practice Desirable Qualifications: Three or more years of Hospitalist experience Online Application Required Documents Curriculum Vitae To start the Online Application process for this position, click the \"Apply for This Position\" button located below the Contact Information. Contact Information Contact: Jennifer E Reed - jennifer-e-reed@uiowa.edu Cmed-Internal Medicine General Hospital 220 Hawkins Drive SE620 GH Iowa City, IA 52242 The University of Iowa is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment free from discrimination on the basis of race, creed, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, pregnancy (including childbirth and related conditions), disability, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, service in the U.S. military, sexual orientation, or associational preferences. Persons with disabilities may contact University Human Resources/Faculty and Staff Disability Services, (319) 335-2660 or fsds@uiowa.edu , to inquire or discuss accommodation needs. Prospective employees may review the University Campus Security Policy and the latest annual crime statistics by contacting the Department of Public Safety at 319/335-5022. The University of Iowa University of Iowa Jobs @ UIowa Iowa City, Iowa 52242 319-335-3500 Footer primary Human Resources Working at a Public University Federal EEO Rights Campus Safety & Security Contact Us © 2026 The University of Iowa Privacy Notice UI Nondiscrimination Statement Accessibility"
